- entry .OpenSsh   OpenSSH's two key formats: the `openssh-key-v1` container and the `authorized_keys` line
+ entry .OpenSsh   die beiden Schlüsselformate von OpenSSH: der Container `openssh-key-v1` und die Zeile in `authorized_keys`

= entry .OpenSsh   OpenSSH's two key formats: the `openssh-key-v1` container and the `authorized_keys` line
-   detail
+   detail

-       The container `ssh-keygen` has written private keys in since OpenSSH 7.8 (armored as
-       `OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY`, which `PrivateKey.pemDecodable` reads through `.privateKey`), and
-       the single line — type, base64 blob, optional comment — which `id_*.pub`,
-       `authorized_keys` and `known_hosts` hold a public key as. Both are built from the SSH
-       wire encoding (RFC 4251 §5); neither is ASN.1, so each is converted to the PKCS#8 or
-       `SubjectPublicKeyInfo` document the providers take. The key types OpenSSH names and this
-       library reads are `ssh-ed25519`, `ssh-rsa` and `ecdsa-sha2-nistp256`/`384`/`521`.
+       Der Container, in den `ssh-keygen` seit OpenSSH 7.8 private Schlüssel schreibt
+       (ASCII-umhüllt als `OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY`, was `PrivateKey.pemDecodable`
+       über `.privateKey` liest), und die einzelne Zeile — Typ, Base64-Blob, optionaler
+       Kommentar —, in der `id_*.pub`, `authorized_keys` und `known_hosts` einen öffentlichen
+       Schlüssel halten. Beide bauen auf der SSH-Übertragungskodierung auf (RFC 4251 §5); keines
+       ist ASN.1, daher wird jedes in das PKCS#8- oder `SubjectPublicKeyInfo`-Dokument
+       umgewandelt, das die Provider entgegennehmen. Die Schlüsseltypen, die OpenSSH nennt und
+       diese Bibliothek liest, sind `ssh-ed25519`, `ssh-rsa` und
+       `ecdsa-sha2-nistp256`/`384`/`521`.

=       library reads are `ssh-ed25519`, `ssh-rsa` and `ecdsa-sha2-nistp256`/`384`/`521`.
